                  <provenance type="#i" cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="">Thetford, Norfolk.
                     Priory of St George, of Benedictine nuns</orgName><p>This attribution was
                     included (with a query) in the second edition of Medieval Libraries of Great
                     Britain (1964). There were no relevant changes in the Supplement (1987).
                     However, the attribution appears to have been accidentally omitted from MLGB3
                     (2010-2015). The corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card
                     (written by Ker) provides the following information: <q><q><persName role="fmo"
                     >Katherina Methwold</persName> monaca</q>. See <title>HMC</title> III, p. 112.
                     A nun of this name was at Thetford in 1492 and 1514 - see <title>Vis. Dioc.
                     Norw.</title> ed. Jessopp (1888), pp. 33, 91.</q></p><p>Compare, more recently,
                     Anne Clark Bartlett, <title>Male Authors, Female Readers Representation and
                     Subjectivity in Middle English Devotional Literature</title> (Ithaca, 1995), p.
                     170, where this manuscript is listed in an appendix entitled 'A descriptive
                     list of extant books owned by medieval English nuns and convents'.
                     </p></provenance>
               </history>
